`twice` answers `i32`, and a `spawn` without a destination stores nothing: a task's answer is kept only by `s.spawn(entry, arg, dst, at)`, which stores it in `dst[at]` when the scope joins, so make the task answer `void` or give it a destination, `s.spawn(twice, arg, out, i)` with `out`, a `i32[]` of one slot per task, declared before the scope's block
